Author: thesa <thesa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Aug 17 15:55:49 2026 -0400

    fix(main,order_executor,execution_log): route cmd_order's live fills through execution_log instead of the paper ledger
    
    cmd_order's live buy/sell fills were unconditionally recorded via
    paper.place_paper_order() and never logged live=True, so a real live
    position was invisible to the automated protective-exit scanner. The next
    cron/watch cycle could then silently "close" it via paper.close_paper_early()
    (which never touches the exchange), leaving the real position open and
    unmanaged indefinitely.
    
    cmd_order now routes live fills through execution_log/LivePositionStore via
    a new shared execution_log.record_live_exit_fill() helper (also refactored
    into order_executor._exit_live_position, a pure behavior-preserving
    refactor). Live orders are placed immediate-or-cancel instead of GTC
    (confirmed via AskUserQuestion) so a resting order can never orphan the fix
    -- no code taught the general poller about closes_position_id.
    
    Two full opus reviews (effort:high) each caught real severe bugs in the
    fix itself, not just the original problem: round 1 found the fix never
    actually worked (Kalshi's real order-status vocabulary has no "filled",
    so the hardcoded status filter downstream never matched a translated raw
    status) plus missing close_time/entry_prob, no quantity clamping, and no
    settled_at concurrency guard -- all fixed. Round 2, reviewing round 1's
    own fixes, found two NEW bugs those fixes introduced: an unmatched live
    sell was recorded in a shape indistinguishable from an open long position
    (worse than the original bug), and a new race-guard exception, uncaught by
    any call site, could crash the entire watch --auto --live process from a
    race on one position. Both fixed.
    
    Mid-session, a concurrent session's own commit (105cf4ce) fixed the sibling
    backlog entry (L1378) in the exact same function -- manually merged so both
    fixes coexist (verified via their tests + this session's new ones together).
    
    Resolves backlog.txt's L1412 entry. Two new follow-up entries filed but
    deliberately not fixed here (same-payload test): the KALSHI_ENV=prod
    startup banner also wrongly claims only watch --auto --live can place live
    orders, and paper.check_position_limits' exposure caps never read
    execution_log for real live positions.
    
    188 tests across the three directly-touched files, 1515 in the wide
    regression sweep, all pass. graphify-out/ refreshed for the touched files.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

